      "lf": 2,
      "text": "name: es-capital-gains"
    },
    {
      "lf": 3,
      "text": "description: Use this Guide to compute Spanish common-territory individual capital gains and losses for 2026. It covers transfer versus non-transfer classification, acquisition and disposal values, fees, improvements, depreciation, homogeneous-security identification, main-home reinvestment, over-65 relief, insured life annuities, pre-1994 abatement, repurchase-deferred losses, annual savings-pool integration and the current savings scale. Trigger phrases include capital gains Spain, ganancia patrimonial, sell shares, property gain, reinversi\u00f3n vivienda habitual, coeficientes de abatimiento, p\u00e9rdida por recompra and compensaci\u00f3n de p\u00e9rdidas. Obtain the actual residence, asset and lot records, prices, eligible costs, prior-loss and repurchase history and relief evidence. The computation uses the taxpayer\u2019s whole annual savings position and minimum allocation rather than taxing each sale through fresh first bands. Non-resident and special incoming-worker cases follow their companion routes."
    },
